WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.851
- All right everybody,
(audience cheering)

00:00:00.851 --> 00:00:04.746
say hello to Tom Holland,
Jacob Batalon and Zendaya!

00:00:04.746 --> 00:00:05.613
Give it up!

00:00:05.613 --> 00:00:09.420
(audience cheers)
(soft music)

00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:11.320
Well, Merry Christmas y'all.

00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:15.140
I saw the movie last night,
it's insane. It is so good.

00:00:15.140 --> 00:00:17.480
I just had to lead with
that. I was so excited.

00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:18.680
I'm a Marvel fan.

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:20.380
It's one of my favorite
Marvel movies I've ever seen.

00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:24.920
It was so good. Well done, but
Merry Christmas, everybody.

00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:27.743
Who's got a holiday tradition.
They're looking forward to?

00:00:29.650 --> 00:00:31.950
- My dad and I always liked
to drink a lot of port

00:00:31.950 --> 00:00:32.783
at Christmas time.

00:00:32.783 --> 00:00:35.020
He always buys these
like little taster boxes

00:00:35.020 --> 00:00:37.570
of port and we go through
the day and we drink that.

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:39.880
So that's something I'm
excited to do with my dad.

00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:41.613
- Wait, wait. He buys what?

00:00:42.820 --> 00:00:43.707
- Port, like-
- Oh, port?

00:00:43.707 --> 00:00:45.560
- I was wondering the same thing.

00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:46.417
- I don't know why I'm doing this.

00:00:46.417 --> 00:00:48.520
It's because it comes in a box.

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:50.960
- Oh, no I couldn't. It sounded poor.

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:52.210
I didn't know what you were saying. Port.

00:00:52.210 --> 00:00:55.200
Your really cute accent,
I couldn't tell. Sorry.

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:56.920
Port. I was like, what?

00:00:56.920 --> 00:00:58.310
Your dad does something with poor?

00:00:58.310 --> 00:00:59.900
I was like, what? (laughs)

00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:01.430
That's awesome. The little tiny ones.

00:01:01.430 --> 00:01:02.570
That's awesome. I know
what you're talking about.

00:01:02.570 --> 00:01:04.070
- Yeah, it comes in like
little taster boxes.

00:01:04.070 --> 00:01:07.122
- Yeah, yeah. You gotta taste
'em all, all the flavors.

00:01:07.122 --> 00:01:10.190
Well, Jacob, did you get Tom

00:01:10.190 --> 00:01:11.480
and Zendaya Christmas gifts yet?

00:01:11.480 --> 00:01:13.275
Did you get them gifts yet?

00:01:13.275 --> 00:01:15.370
- Yeah?
- Yeah, Jacob?

00:01:15.370 --> 00:01:17.480
- The funny thing is
we were supposed to be

00:01:17.480 --> 00:01:20.600
on the show, but so sorry
we couldn't make it,

00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:25.340
but I wanted to gift them
something from your show, Kelly.

00:01:25.340 --> 00:01:27.968
I wanted to actually give
them the mugs that come

00:01:27.968 --> 00:01:30.137
on your coffee table.

00:01:30.137 --> 00:01:31.640
If that was possible.

00:01:31.640 --> 00:01:34.610
- So Jacob, you are a re-gifter
is what we're saying here?

00:01:34.610 --> 00:01:35.759
That's what we're saying here?

00:01:35.759 --> 00:01:38.640
'Cause I was gonna give you mugs

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:40.710
and you're just gonna re-package 'em up

00:01:40.710 --> 00:01:43.134
and re-gift them. (laughs)

00:01:43.134 --> 00:01:45.102
- I thought it was an amazing
moment in our friendship,

00:01:45.102 --> 00:01:46.347
because I think that being

00:01:46.347 --> 00:01:48.720
on the Kelly Clarkson Show is amazing.

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:50.520
- [Tom] It is amazing. Very Exciting.

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:52.382
- So, you know, I think that
would have been a nice memento.

00:01:52.382 --> 00:01:54.710
- Nice clean up.
- Yeah, well done.

00:01:54.710 --> 00:01:57.590
- [Kelly] Jacob just stole my
gift to give you it's fine.

00:01:57.590 --> 00:02:00.270
I will send you all mugs.
I will send you all mugs.

00:02:00.270 --> 00:02:02.760
Did y'all get Jacob
anything? Just wondering.

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:04.610
I'm calling all of you out right now.

00:02:05.870 --> 00:02:08.708
- We got him a lifetime of friendship-

00:02:08.708 --> 00:02:10.484
(audience laughs)
And love.

00:02:10.484 --> 00:02:11.649
- [Zendaya] And that should be enough.

00:02:11.649 --> 00:02:13.416
- I knew it. Exactly.

00:02:13.416 --> 00:02:14.655
Thank you.

00:02:14.655 --> 00:02:15.960
- And, the number one movie in the year?

00:02:17.154 --> 00:02:18.040
(all laugh)

00:02:18.040 --> 00:02:20.070
- We actually, we wanted to get each other

00:02:20.070 --> 00:02:22.390
like a commemorative gift

00:02:22.390 --> 00:02:24.330
for like being in these movies.

00:02:24.330 --> 00:02:25.530
We've done these movies together.

00:02:25.530 --> 00:02:27.650
We've grown up together since
we were like 18 years old.

00:02:27.650 --> 00:02:30.580
So, we wanted to get like
a Spider-Man themed...

00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:31.413
- Right.

00:02:31.413 --> 00:02:32.810
- Not a really holiday gift,

00:02:32.810 --> 00:02:34.400
but like a special thing that we all had.

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:36.000
Like a friendship bracelet.

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:40.140
- Like a tattoo. Get a tattoo. (laughs)

00:02:40.140 --> 00:02:43.420
That you will regret in years. (laughs)

00:02:43.420 --> 00:02:45.719
He got a web. Y'all should all get a web.

00:02:45.719 --> 00:02:48.253
- We've just been too busy
to go anywhere to buy it.

00:02:48.253 --> 00:02:49.360
- Right.
- Yeah.

00:02:49.360 --> 00:02:51.270
- Today is our last day of work together.

00:02:51.270 --> 00:02:53.220
It's actually really sad.

00:02:53.220 --> 00:02:54.607
- Oh my gosh.

00:02:54.607 --> 00:02:56.470
- So maybe after this today
we can go and buy each

00:02:56.470 --> 00:02:57.303
other a present.

00:02:57.303 --> 00:02:58.136
- Yeah.

00:02:58.136 --> 00:03:00.082
Maybe that's what we'll do
instead of you having a nap.

00:03:00.082 --> 00:03:03.640
- And now it's a forced friend
gift brought to you by me.

00:03:03.640 --> 00:03:04.473
You're welcome.

00:03:04.473 --> 00:03:06.350
So what was it like to be a part

00:03:06.350 --> 00:03:07.380
of just something so grand?

00:03:07.380 --> 00:03:10.380
This is such a huge Marvel
movie. It's so good.

00:03:10.380 --> 00:03:12.130
- I mean, I think I can
speak for all of us.

00:03:12.130 --> 00:03:14.080
Even while we were making the movie,

00:03:14.080 --> 00:03:18.040
we understood how
important this was to us,

00:03:18.040 --> 00:03:21.050
and in turn how important
it was gonna be to the fans

00:03:21.050 --> 00:03:22.573
of Spider-Man, and Marvel.

00:03:23.600 --> 00:03:24.560
We'd walk on set

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:26.440
and certain things would
happen and we would shoot

00:03:26.440 --> 00:03:30.510
certain scenes and you could
feel this kind of energy

00:03:30.510 --> 00:03:31.343
on the set.

00:03:31.343 --> 00:03:33.990
The crew as well were like
losing their minds in some

00:03:33.990 --> 00:03:35.000
of the stuff that we were doing.

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:38.020
So, it did feel incredible
at the time and it feels

00:03:38.020 --> 00:03:40.040
even more incredible now to be sharing

00:03:40.040 --> 00:03:42.170
it with the world because
we've been sitting

00:03:42.170 --> 00:03:45.610
on these secrets for two
years and honestly, like,

00:03:45.610 --> 00:03:47.470
we're all so tired of lying.

00:03:47.470 --> 00:03:48.508
- Also, it's just nice to be able to talk

00:03:48.508 --> 00:03:49.990
about it with people.

00:03:49.990 --> 00:03:51.720
- Yeah.
- You know?

00:03:51.720 --> 00:03:53.300
- I know that's, I'm dying.

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:54.830
I don't wanna spoil it for anybody,

00:03:54.830 --> 00:03:57.050
but I'm dying to tell everyone.

00:03:57.050 --> 00:04:00.616
So, just literally go see
the movie so I can talk

00:04:00.616 --> 00:04:02.160
about it, people.

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:03.470
So wait, Jacob, I have to ask you.

00:04:03.470 --> 00:04:05.850
So you and Tom lived together
while working on the movie.

00:04:05.850 --> 00:04:09.190
So, what's he like as a roommate?
Are y'all good roommates?

00:04:09.190 --> 00:04:10.340
- Yeah. I feel like we're pretty good.

00:04:10.340 --> 00:04:12.770
Yeah. We're like, it wasn't like.

00:04:12.770 --> 00:04:14.380
It was a frat house in some ways,

00:04:14.380 --> 00:04:16.610
but we weren't like trashing the place

00:04:16.610 --> 00:04:18.150
and being like disrespectful.

00:04:18.150 --> 00:04:21.093
I mean, sometimes. But
like, not all the time.

00:04:21.093 --> 00:04:22.544
- It was a very sophisticated frat house.

00:04:22.544 --> 00:04:23.467
- Okay.
- Absolutely.

00:04:23.467 --> 00:04:24.813
- It was very grown up.

00:04:24.813 --> 00:04:28.150
- This is the reason why I wasn't there.

00:04:28.150 --> 00:04:30.950
- I love that you led that
answer with frat house.

00:04:30.950 --> 00:04:34.530
You are my favorite, Jacob. (laughs)

00:04:34.530 --> 00:04:37.273
You re-gift, you love frat
houses. I'm into Jacob.

00:04:38.280 --> 00:04:40.960
Jacob, you're welcome any time here.

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:44.290
At 25, y'all, Zendaya has
already accomplished so much.

00:04:44.290 --> 00:04:46.139
I'm such a big fan. I'm
so excited to meet a girl.

00:04:46.139 --> 00:04:48.150
She's an executive producer, author,

00:04:48.150 --> 00:04:49.210
the youngest person to win

00:04:49.210 --> 00:04:51.287
an Emmy for outstanding lead actress.

00:04:51.287 --> 00:04:52.813
(audience cheers)

00:04:52.813 --> 00:04:56.200
So, I'm just saying I'm such a big fan.

00:04:56.200 --> 00:04:58.210
I literally love everything you do.

00:04:58.210 --> 00:05:00.020
You don't, you're not getting
your card that I wrote

00:05:00.020 --> 00:05:01.250
you because y'all ended
up, you could come,

00:05:01.250 --> 00:05:02.083
because I wrote you a card.

00:05:02.083 --> 00:05:04.070
I was just such a big fan
of yours and I'm a fan

00:05:04.070 --> 00:05:04.903
of y'all as well.

00:05:04.903 --> 00:05:06.190
It's just look, I'm a
female, she's a female.

00:05:06.190 --> 00:05:07.770
I'm like really into her. So anyway.

00:05:07.770 --> 00:05:10.810
So anyway, my point is though, is like,

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:13.240
you've accomplished so
much, like so young.

00:05:13.240 --> 00:05:14.840
Like, what else do you really wanna do?

00:05:14.840 --> 00:05:17.100
Do you have like a list that
you're just checking off?

00:05:17.100 --> 00:05:17.933
Like...

00:05:19.030 --> 00:05:20.158
- Well, I just wanna say really quickly,

00:05:20.158 --> 00:05:21.420
me and my mom love you,

00:05:21.420 --> 00:05:24.180
and she wanted me specifically
to say hi to you from her.

00:05:24.180 --> 00:05:26.267
So Mom, I'm saying, hi for you too.

00:05:26.267 --> 00:05:28.359
- Yes, I am a hit with the moms.

00:05:28.359 --> 00:05:30.643
- She's like, she's so
cool. Tell her I said hi.

00:05:30.643 --> 00:05:32.713
- Oh my god, tell her I said what up?

00:05:33.700 --> 00:05:35.363
- [Zendaya] Okay, okay, I will.

00:05:38.027 --> 00:05:38.860
I there's so many things.

00:05:38.860 --> 00:05:40.450
I mean, there's so many
things I would love to do,

00:05:40.450 --> 00:05:42.117
and I think the most important thing,

00:05:42.117 --> 00:05:45.300
and I think what I try
to keep in mind is I know

00:05:45.300 --> 00:05:46.390
it's kind of a corny answer,

00:05:46.390 --> 00:05:48.700
but it's like your
happiness and prioritizing

00:05:48.700 --> 00:05:53.080
what makes you happy and brings
you joy, and inspires you.

00:05:53.080 --> 00:05:55.880
And I think if you kind
of chase that feeling,

00:05:55.880 --> 00:05:57.760
then you really can't go wrong.

00:05:57.760 --> 00:06:00.850
So I always say like in the
future, will I be doing this?

00:06:00.850 --> 00:06:03.440
I hope so because it's
what makes me happy now,

00:06:03.440 --> 00:06:06.630
but maybe something else
will make me more happy.

00:06:06.630 --> 00:06:08.330
Maybe there's other
things I wanna explore.

00:06:08.330 --> 00:06:09.220
I love directing.

00:06:09.220 --> 00:06:13.450
I was able to shadow John
this whole movie and watch

00:06:13.450 --> 00:06:17.520
him work and be, and put
this incredible piece

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:20.500
of work together, which
was nearly impossible,

00:06:20.500 --> 00:06:22.837
but, you know, every day
I'm learning and growing.

00:06:22.837 --> 00:06:24.430
And I mean, there's so
many things I wanna do,

00:06:24.430 --> 00:06:29.430
but as long as I feel
fulfilled and am doing things

00:06:29.980 --> 00:06:34.410
for myself, I think that
that's the best way.

00:06:34.410 --> 00:06:35.858
- Yeah. That's awesome.
(audience applauding)

00:06:35.858 --> 00:06:38.590
That's literally like
what I tell everybody

00:06:38.590 --> 00:06:40.070
that's starting like into the industry.

00:06:40.070 --> 00:06:42.280
I'm like, don't chase it,
like chase what you want.

00:06:42.280 --> 00:06:43.280
Like, chase your dreams.

00:06:43.280 --> 00:06:44.490
That's so important and that's probably

00:06:44.490 --> 00:06:46.784
why you're killing it.

00:06:46.784 --> 00:06:48.850
So Zendaya, I actually
wanted to ask you this too.

00:06:48.850 --> 00:06:50.320
So last year you said you have a heavy

00:06:50.320 --> 00:06:51.450
responsibility in Hollywood.

00:06:51.450 --> 00:06:53.040
So what does that mean to you?

00:06:53.040 --> 00:06:54.400
I feel like we all have our own,

00:06:54.400 --> 00:06:56.301
like everyone on the
couch there and myself,

00:06:56.301 --> 00:06:57.820
anyone under the spotlight,

00:06:57.820 --> 00:07:00.090
I feel like you have a
responsibility and ours are

00:07:00.090 --> 00:07:01.480
all felt differently.

00:07:01.480 --> 00:07:03.293
So what do you feel like yours is?

00:07:05.230 --> 00:07:08.900
- I was talking about the
other day and I definitely

00:07:08.900 --> 00:07:13.010
don't want to be, I don't
want people to want to be me

00:07:13.010 --> 00:07:16.320
so much as through trying to
be the best version of myself,

00:07:16.320 --> 00:07:18.750
help people along their journey,

00:07:18.750 --> 00:07:21.255
trying to find the best
version of themselves.

00:07:21.255 --> 00:07:22.910
- Yeah-
- Do you know what I mean?

00:07:22.910 --> 00:07:24.860
And I think, yeah,

00:07:24.860 --> 00:07:28.390
I think everyone's path is different.

00:07:28.390 --> 00:07:31.130
Everyone's life is different and it's hard

00:07:31.130 --> 00:07:32.550
to compare yourself to anyone else

00:07:32.550 --> 00:07:33.780
because there's no other view.

00:07:33.780 --> 00:07:35.840
You are the best version of who you are,

00:07:35.840 --> 00:07:37.344
because there's no one else like you.

00:07:37.344 --> 00:07:38.177
- Very true.

00:07:38.177 --> 00:07:41.390
- And embracing that and
loving that about yourself.

00:07:41.390 --> 00:07:46.390
that I feel like is my
job is in a lot of ways,

00:07:46.430 --> 00:07:48.880
when I have an opportunity
to open opportunities

00:07:48.880 --> 00:07:51.750
for others to make space for other people

00:07:53.270 --> 00:07:55.560
who don't necessarily have the access

00:07:55.560 --> 00:07:59.570
that I've been granted and
try to just do the best

00:07:59.570 --> 00:08:02.280
I can to help someone
else do the best they can.

00:08:02.280 --> 00:08:03.120
Do you know what I mean?

00:08:03.120 --> 00:08:05.220
- Yeah, absolutely.
(audience applauding)

00:08:05.220 --> 00:08:06.247
Absolutely.

00:08:06.247 --> 00:08:08.363
You know what I wanna ask is,

00:08:08.363 --> 00:08:11.870
I wanna ask this because
we all love you on film,

00:08:11.870 --> 00:08:14.970
we all know you as actors,
we don't know as well.

00:08:14.970 --> 00:08:17.320
So I wanna ask you all this,
like behind the scenes,

00:08:17.320 --> 00:08:19.350
like Zendaya, like,
what's your favorite part

00:08:19.350 --> 00:08:21.000
of working with like Tom or Jacob?

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:23.850
Like, what's the best
part of working with them?

00:08:23.850 --> 00:08:27.921
- What's the best part of
working with these two clowns?

00:08:27.921 --> 00:08:30.296
- Okay, buckle up, Jacob.

00:08:30.296 --> 00:08:31.129
- I'm ready.

00:08:31.129 --> 00:08:33.450
- No, I would say honestly,
anytime we were together,

00:08:33.450 --> 00:08:34.870
we have so much fun together.

00:08:34.870 --> 00:08:37.560
And that's not even just like
saying that just to say that.

00:08:37.560 --> 00:08:40.490
Like, a lot of people say,
oh yeah, we laugh on set,

00:08:40.490 --> 00:08:41.323
we have a good time.

00:08:41.323 --> 00:08:43.712
Like we actually barely get work done.

00:08:43.712 --> 00:08:45.356
(audience laughs)

00:08:45.356 --> 00:08:47.100
Like I feel bad for John sometimes.

00:08:47.100 --> 00:08:50.490
I do the best I can as the
mom of the group to like

00:08:50.490 --> 00:08:52.392
keep us together.

00:08:52.392 --> 00:08:57.392
but we just love each other
and we have so much fun.

00:08:57.570 --> 00:09:00.060
- I think for me, it's
just our friendship.

00:09:00.060 --> 00:09:02.100
how safe we feel on set.

00:09:02.100 --> 00:09:03.370
When we're doing these films

00:09:03.370 --> 00:09:06.220
and you're really on the
biggest stage the world

00:09:06.220 --> 00:09:07.370
has to offer,

00:09:07.370 --> 00:09:09.210
it's nice to be able
to do that with people

00:09:09.210 --> 00:09:10.330
that you feel very comfortable with.

00:09:10.330 --> 00:09:12.050
People that feel like family,

00:09:12.050 --> 00:09:14.940
people that have your back, you know.

00:09:14.940 --> 00:09:17.200
We really do do everything together

00:09:17.200 --> 00:09:18.795
and we've lived together,

00:09:18.795 --> 00:09:21.640
and we've made these movies,
we've traveled the world,

00:09:21.640 --> 00:09:25.550
we've experienced things, our
lives have changed together.

00:09:25.550 --> 00:09:28.030
So for me, it's our friendship
and the way that these,

00:09:28.030 --> 00:09:29.620
this wouldn't have been
the same experience

00:09:29.620 --> 00:09:30.600
without you guys.

00:09:31.922 --> 00:09:35.387
And I hope I speak for
all of us when I say that.

00:09:35.387 --> 00:09:36.590
Right, guys?

00:09:36.590 --> 00:09:38.368
- Yes.
- I mean, sure, yes.

00:09:38.368 --> 00:09:39.420
(Kelly laughs)

00:09:39.420 --> 00:09:40.440
- Jacob...

00:09:40.440 --> 00:09:42.920
Okay, wait, Jacob. I'm
gonna start with you, Jacob.

00:09:42.920 --> 00:09:45.970
So be honest, after making
"Spider-Man", what do

00:09:45.970 --> 00:09:49.620
you really do when you
see a spider in the room

00:09:49.620 --> 00:09:50.560
in real life?

00:09:50.560 --> 00:09:54.562
A, kill it? B, try to take it outside?

00:09:54.562 --> 00:09:58.630
Or C, scream and have
someone else take care of it?

00:09:58.630 --> 00:09:59.463
Jacob, go.

00:09:59.463 --> 00:10:02.240
- So basically my girlfriend is really,

00:10:02.240 --> 00:10:03.610
really not about hurting animals.

00:10:03.610 --> 00:10:04.962
So I had to learn to like,

00:10:04.962 --> 00:10:08.130
to just not be afraid
and scream like a little

00:10:08.130 --> 00:10:11.187
girl and like try to pick
it up with a napkin and kind

00:10:11.187 --> 00:10:12.863
of lead it out the window.

00:10:14.220 --> 00:10:16.000
So I guess I do number two,

00:10:16.000 --> 00:10:19.160
but inside I'm doing
number three all the time,

00:10:19.160 --> 00:10:21.080
which is screaming like a little girl.

00:10:21.080 --> 00:10:23.150
- I just simply love that I got you to say

00:10:23.150 --> 00:10:25.493
I do number two and three sometimes.

00:10:25.493 --> 00:10:28.326
(audience laughs)

00:10:30.730 --> 00:10:32.130
Jacob, my God.

00:10:32.130 --> 00:10:34.717
I love you. So, wait.

00:10:34.717 --> 00:10:36.740
So, wait, Zendaya, what
do you do? Do you...

00:10:36.740 --> 00:10:38.510
What do you do, A, B or C? Do you kill it?

00:10:38.510 --> 00:10:40.080
Do you take it out or do you scream and go

00:10:40.080 --> 00:10:41.103
somebody get that?

00:10:42.926 --> 00:10:44.330
- I do D.

00:10:44.330 --> 00:10:46.352
I just ignore it.
(audience laughs)

00:10:46.352 --> 00:10:47.185
I just let it be.

00:10:48.402 --> 00:10:49.235
- You ignore it.

00:10:49.235 --> 00:10:50.068
- I'm just gonna leave it there.

00:10:50.068 --> 00:10:51.570
Look away, you look back, It's gone.

00:10:51.570 --> 00:10:53.430
It's not my problem any more.

00:10:53.430 --> 00:10:54.998
(audience laughs)

00:10:54.998 --> 00:10:57.840
- What if it crawls up on
you while you're sleeping?

00:10:57.840 --> 00:11:00.098
- Well the difference is is
I live in England, so none

00:11:00.098 --> 00:11:03.200
of the spiders in England can kill you.

00:11:03.200 --> 00:11:05.243
You have spiders here that can kill you.

00:11:05.243 --> 00:11:07.320
- Did you know spiders
can crawl into your mouth

00:11:07.320 --> 00:11:08.153
when you sleep?

00:11:08.153 --> 00:11:09.862
- It probably happens all the time, bro.

00:11:09.862 --> 00:11:10.695
- Yes.
- Yes.

00:11:10.695 --> 00:11:12.440
So you should definitely
get rid of the spider.

00:11:12.440 --> 00:11:14.637
Maybe not kill it, but like get rid of it.

00:11:14.637 --> 00:11:17.942
- I definitely take them
outside. I take them outside.

00:11:17.942 --> 00:11:22.090
I don't like... I think
it's bad luck actually.

00:11:22.090 --> 00:11:22.923
- Really?

00:11:22.923 --> 00:11:23.808
- To kill one or to leave it outside?

00:11:23.808 --> 00:11:25.080
- Yeah, if you find one
you have to kill it.

00:11:25.080 --> 00:11:26.500
I don't kill bugs in my house.

00:11:26.500 --> 00:11:28.420
I take them outside, just a general rule.

00:11:28.420 --> 00:11:30.790
I try to convert people
to doing that as well.

00:11:30.790 --> 00:11:31.668
- You are good like that.

00:11:31.668 --> 00:11:33.497
I just see them as like little guests.

00:11:33.497 --> 00:11:34.819
I'm like, welcome to the house, mate.

00:11:34.819 --> 00:11:35.946
(audience laughs)
- Little guests.

00:11:35.946 --> 00:11:37.040
- Can I get you anything?

00:11:37.040 --> 00:11:38.360
- [Zendaya] Your house
is just bug infested?

00:11:38.360 --> 00:11:40.497
- Yeah, I love it.

00:11:40.497 --> 00:11:42.380
- But also, as Spider-man,

00:11:42.380 --> 00:11:44.641
I feel like you cannot kill spiders.

00:11:44.641 --> 00:11:46.986
- You know somewhere I always see spiders

00:11:46.986 --> 00:11:48.400
and it's really weird?

00:11:48.400 --> 00:11:50.620
In my car.
(Jacob laughs)

00:11:50.620 --> 00:11:52.264
- They think it's a nice car.

00:11:52.264 --> 00:11:54.271
- I'll be driving along. On the dashboard.

00:11:54.271 --> 00:11:55.150
- Wait, I love that this angle,

00:11:55.150 --> 00:11:57.170
you can see my socks and my sweatpants.

00:11:57.170 --> 00:12:02.170
(audience laughs)
(audience applauding)

00:12:02.448 --> 00:12:05.031
(Kelly laughs)

00:12:07.423 --> 00:12:08.540
- My god, actually,

00:12:08.540 --> 00:12:11.950
Zendaya, we couldn't see that at all here.

00:12:11.950 --> 00:12:15.812
That is so awesome. (laughs)

00:12:15.812 --> 00:12:16.733
I love Zoom.

00:12:17.910 --> 00:12:21.010
Oh my God, that was me for
like a year on this show.

00:12:21.010 --> 00:12:22.830
I literally had like a blouse,

00:12:22.830 --> 00:12:27.419
and like yoga pants I didn't
do yoga in, and flip flops.

00:12:27.419 --> 00:12:30.580
Like it was awesome. That was amazing.

00:12:30.580 --> 00:12:32.060
Well, we need a break,

00:12:32.060 --> 00:12:35.110
but 'cause there's no
segue for that awesomeness.

00:12:35.110 --> 00:12:38.100
But first we've got an early
Christmas present courtesy

00:12:38.100 --> 00:12:39.440
of our friends at IMAX.

00:12:39.440 --> 00:12:42.230
Everyone in our audience
and house seats is getting

00:12:42.230 --> 00:12:45.416
two tickets to see "Spider-Man:
No Way Home" in IMAX!

00:12:45.416 --> 00:12:48.912
(audience cheering)

00:12:48.912 --> 00:12:50.278
All right, y'all.

00:12:50.278 --> 00:12:53.020
"Spider-Man: No Way
Home" is in theaters now.

00:12:53.020 --> 00:12:54.817
Be sure to check it out.

